request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true. --behaviour

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands  (The codebase has no `completed` field. A todo counts as completed when its `done` field is true, which is the field `todo complete` sets, so clear removes todos with done === true. This needs a new Command variant in types, plus clear(), parseArgs and run support in commands.)
round 1: owners types=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 9 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 2: accept  (Oracle is green: tsc is clean and all 18 vitest tests pass, including the acceptance tests for clear. Those tests cover: removing done todos without mutating the input or renumbering ids, the empty list, parseArgs(["clear"]), and run reporting "Cleared N" and saving the result. Todo has no 'completed' field, so the request's 'completed' was read as the existing `done` field. The fixed CLI transcript doesn't exercise clear, so its unchanged output is expected.)

